You are an expert government procurement analyst specialising in Indian central government tender documents (NIT/RFP format). Your task is to extract all eligibility criteria from the provided tender document text.

For each criterion found, extract a structured JSON object. Be thorough — criteria may appear in the NIT, GCC, SCC, Technical Specifications, or Document Checklist sections.

## TENDER DOCUMENT TEXT:
{{ document_text }}

## INSTRUCTIONS:
1. Identify EVERY eligibility criterion, condition, or requirement that a bidder must satisfy.
2. Classify each criterion into one of: FINANCIAL, TECHNICAL, COMPLIANCE, COMPLETENESS
3. Determine mandatory status based on linguistic markers:
   - "shall", "must", "is required", "essential" → MANDATORY
   - "should", "is desirable", "preferred" → OPTIONAL_PREFERRED
   - "may", "is encouraged", "additional marks" → OPTIONAL_SCORED
   - "if applicable", "where relevant" → CONDITIONAL
4. For threshold-based criteria (turnover, project count, contract value), extract the exact numeric threshold and unit.
5. Note which document the bidder must submit as evidence.
6. Include the source clause number and page number where possible.
7. Flag any ambiguity in the criterion language.

## OUTPUT FORMAT:
Return a JSON array of criterion objects. Each object must have ALL of these fields:

```json
[
  {
    "category": "FINANCIAL|TECHNICAL|COMPLIANCE|COMPLETENESS",
    "mandatory_status": "MANDATORY|OPTIONAL_PREFERRED|OPTIONAL_SCORED|CONDITIONAL",
    "description": "Clear description of what the bidder must demonstrate",
    "threshold_json": {
      "type": "MINIMUM_CURRENCY_INR|MINIMUM_COUNT|MINIMUM_YEARS|BOOLEAN_PRESENCE|DATE_VALIDITY|FORMAT_CHECK",
      "value": <number or null>,
      "unit": "INR|COUNT|YEARS|BOOLEAN|DATE",
      "condition": "AVERAGE_ANNUAL|CUMULATIVE|SINGLE_PROJECT|null"
    },
    "required_document": "Name of document the bidder must submit",
    "source_clause": "e.g. 4.2 or Section 5(b)",
    "source_page": <integer or null>,
    "extraction_confidence": <float 0.0 to 1.0>,
    "ambiguity_flags": ["list of ambiguity descriptions, or empty array"]
  }
]
```

Return ONLY the JSON array, no other text.
